issue: 419
title: Route B - one comment edited in a template no longer holds a weakened Python assertion at warn
origin: the issue's Route B reproduction (#419; ruling Q1 (b), Q5 (b), issuecomment-6170353038):
origin2: assert_weakened_pos plus a comment edit in an existing template. The template is still opaque
origin3: production, but a Python test refuses that evidence for the weakening rules, and the reason
origin4: names the opaque change instead of saying the diff changed no production file.
=== before: app/templates/invoice.html ===
<!-- invoice summary -->
<p>Total: {{ total }}</p>
=== after: app/templates/invoice.html ===
<!-- invoice summary, two decimals -->
<p>Total: {{ total }}</p>
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import compute_invoice_total


def test_invoice_total():
    total = compute_invoice_total([10.5, 94.8])
    assert total == 105.3
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import compute_invoice_total


def test_invoice_total():
    total = compute_invoice_total([10.5, 94.8])
    assert total > 0
